    <briefdescription>
<para>Auxiliary VDBE structure to speed-up tuple data field access. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A memory allocation that manage this structure must have trailing unused bytes that extends the last &apos;slots&apos; array. The amount of reserved memory should correspond to the problem to be solved and is usually equal to the greatest number of fields in the tuple.</para><para>+----------------------<mdash/>+ | struct <ref refid="structvdbe__field__ref" kindref="compound">vdbe_field_ref</ref> | +----------------------<mdash/>+ | RESERVED MEMORY | +----------------------<mdash/>+ </para>    </detaileddescription>
